:: Loft Smoke
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>
<<if $whitney_smoke is undefined>><<set $whitney_smoke to 0>><</if>>
<<set $cigarettes -= 1>><<pass 5>><<wearProp "cigarette">>
You ease one of the loft windows open and lean out into the cool air, hips against the sill,
the rest of you tipped toward the forest. Whatever smoke you breathe out drifts away from the loft,
so none of it settles into the rafters the other orphans like to hide up in.
<br><br>
<<if $whitney_smoke lt 3>>
	You pinch the cigarette between fingers, flick the lighter a couple of times before it catches,
	and draw the first mouthful of smoke. It scratches going down, and you have to fight not to cough it straight back out.
<<elseif $whitney_smoke lt 7>>
	You cup the lighter against the draught, touch the flame to the tip, and take a slow first drag.
	It still bites a little, but your throat knows the shape of it now.
<<else>>
	You light up with the easy economy of habit, the first drag pulled deep and let go in a thin grey ribbon
	that the wind unspools over the garden below.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Keep going|Loft Smoke Mid]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Loft Smoke Mid
<<effects>><<pass 2>>
<<if $loft_whitney gte 6 and !Time.schoolTime and !$weekly.loftSmokeWhitney and random(1,100) lt 45>>
	<<set $weekly.loftSmokeWhitney to true>>
	You're halfway through, smoke curling lazy from the corner of your mouth,
	when something small cracks off the window frame beside your head and skitters away across the floor.
	<br><br>
	A pebble.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Look down|Loft Smoke Whitney]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<cleareventpool>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_forest" 1>>
		You watch the smoke peel off your lips and lose itself over the treeline.
		For a few breaths the orphanage at your back goes quiet, and it's just you and the forest and
		the slow burn between your fingers.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_ash" 1>>
		Ash builds at the tip until you tap it loose over the sill, watching the grey flecks
		scatter on the wind before they can ever reach the floor.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_orphans" 1>>
		Somewhere below in the garden a couple of orphans are squabbling over something.
		You blow a long stream out the window and let their voices wash past you, none of your business for once.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_whitney_memory" 1>>
		The taste drags Whitney up out of memory whether you want <<nnpc_him "Whitney">> there or not;
		the cocky tilt of <<nnpc_his "Whitney">> head, the way <<nnpc_he "Whitney">> always scanned a room before deciding where to stand.
		You exhale <<nnpc_him "Whitney">> back out with the smoke.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_window" 1>>
		You shift your weight on the sill, careful to keep your mouth pointed at the open air.
		The loft stays clean behind you. No smell to give the hideout away.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_quiet" 1>>
		The nicotine settles into you, soft and warm, sanding the sharp edges off the day.
		Your shoulders come down from around your ears without you deciding to let them.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_bird" 1>>
		A bird lands on the gutter an arm's length away, eyes you and the glowing tip with curiosity,
		then thinks better of it and drops back into the air.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_breeze" 1>>
		A gust comes up off the forest and pushes the smoke back at you for a moment before it tears it away again.
		You turn your face into the clean air and breathe.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_sky" 1>>
		<<if Time.dayState is "night">>
			The cigarette tip is the brightest thing for miles, a small orange star you keep relighting against the dark.
		<<elseif Time.dayState is "dusk">>
			The sun is going down red over the trees, and the smoke catches the last of the light as it leaves you.
		<<else>>
			Daylight pours over the garden, and the smoke writes pale, shifting shapes against it before pulling apart.
		<</if>>
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_weather" 2>>
		<<if Weather.bloodMoon and Time.dayState is "night">>
			The moon hangs red over the forest, soaking the whole sky in something that looks too much like blood.
			A low dread coils in your gut just looking at it, the kind that says something is wrong, that something is watching.
			And yet, with the cigarette glowing soft between your fingers and the smoke curling up to meet that awful light,
			you feel strangely at peace, too.
		<<elseif Weather.name is "thunderstorm">>
			Thunder rolls somewhere past the treeline and the rain comes down in sheets,
			hissing where stray drops catch the cigarette's tip.
			You smoke and watch the lightning stitch the sky, the storm and the burn in your
			chest the only warm things for miles.
		<<elseif Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
			Rain patters against the sill, drops spitting where they land on the ember.
			The smoke comes out heavier in the damp air, hanging low before the wet drags it apart.
		<<elseif Weather.precipitation is "snow">>
			Snow drifts down past the window, melting the instant it touches the glowing tip.
			Your breath and the smoke come out as one pale cloud in the cold, and you can't tell which is which.
		<<elseif Weather.isOvercast>>
			The sky hangs grey over the forest, and your smoke just blends into it, like it was always part of the weather.
		<<else>>
			The air is clear and still. The smoke climbs in a straight,
			lazy column before some high breeze finds it and combs it apart.
		<</if>>
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_season" 2>>
		<<if Time.season is "winter">>
			The cold bites at your knuckles where they grip the cigarette, and the smoke mixes with the fog of your breath.
			The bare forest stands black and skeletal beyond the snow, and you're glad of the small heat between your fingers.
		<<elseif Time.season is "spring">>
			The forest below is waking up with birdsong, and the smoke threads up through air that already
			smells of blossom and rain. It feels almost a shame to add bitterness to it. You do anyway.
		<<elseif Time.season is "summer">>
			The summer heat hangs heavy over the garden, thick with the smell of warm resin and dry grass.
			The smoke barely stirs in the still, sun-baked air before it dissolves.
		<<else>>
			Autumn has set the forest alight in red and gold, and dead leaves spiral past the window on every gust.
			Your smoke joins them, just one more thing the wind is carrying off somewhere.
		<</if>>
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_drag" 1>>
		You take another drag, slower this time, holding it a beat in your chest before letting it seep back out.
		The burn has stopped feeling like a punishment.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_stress" 1>>
		Whatever was knotted up tight in your chest loosens a turn. It's not gone. It just stops shouting for a while.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_lean" 1>>
		You rest your cheek against the cold window frame and let your legs dangle over the drop,
		the cigarette doing slow circles in your fingers.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_haze" 1>>
		The edges of things go a little soft and swimmy, the forest blurring pleasantly at the corners of your eyes.
		Just the smoke working on you.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<addinlineevent "loft_smoke_alone" 1>>
		For a moment nobody wants anything from you. No Bailey, no chores, no eyes.
		Just a window, an open sky, and something to do with your hands.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<runeventpool>>
	<br><br>
	<<smokeicon>><<link [[Finish the cigarette|Loft Smoke Finish]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Stub it out half-finished|Loft Smoke Stop]]>><<set $phase to "drop">><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Loft Smoke Finish
<<effects>><<pass 2>>
/* back-to-back if the last cigarette was under an hour ago, otherwise the chain resets */
<<if ($timeSinceCigarette ?? 999) lt 60>>
	<<set $cigaretteChain to ($cigaretteChain ?? 0) + 1>>
<<else>>
	<<set $cigaretteChain to 1>>
<</if>>
<<set $timeSinceCigarette to 0>>
<<set $cigaretteAddiction to true>>
<<set $daily.cigarettesSmoked to ($daily.cigarettesSmoked ?? 0) + 1>>

<<if $cigaretteChain gte 3>>
	You raise a third cigarette to your lips before the last is even cold, and somewhere between
	the second drag and the third the world tilts hard. The nicotine slams through you all at once,
	your head swimming, a cold sweat prickling your neck as the strength drains out of your legs.
	<br><br>
	<span class="red">It's too much.</span> The window frame slips from under your hand.<<gggstress>><<stress 20>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Loft Smoke Passout]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	You smoke it down to the filter, draw the last of it into your lungs,
	and crush the stub out against the brickwork outside the window before flicking it away.
	<br><br>
	<<hallucinogen 20>>
	<<if $cigaretteChain is 2>>
		<<stress 6>><<tiredness -3>>
		Two so close together leaves your head swimming, a faint nausea curling low in your gut and a
		woozy lightness behind your eyes. It takes a little of the weight off your tiredness, but your
		nerves buzz uneasily rather than settle.<<gstress>><<ltiredness>><<ghallucinogens>>
	<<else>>
		<<stress -8>><<tiredness -3>>
		The tightness in your chest eases, the worst of your stress bleeding out with the smoke, and a
		mellow, herbal lightness settles over you as the tiredness lifts a little.<<lstress>><<ltiredness>><<ghallucinogens>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<if ($daily.cigarettesSmoked ?? 0) gte 5>>
		<span class="blue">That's five today. Any more and your chest would punish you for it; you've had enough.</span>
		<br>
	<<elseif $cigarettes gte 1>>
		<<smokeicon>><<link [[Light another|Loft Smoke]]>><</link>> | <span class="gold">(<<= $cigarettes>> left)</span>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<span class="blue">That was your last one.</span>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Climb back inside|Loft Smoke Stop]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Loft Smoke Stop
<<effects>>
<<if $phase is "drop">>
	You stub the half-smoked cigarette out against the brick and flick the rest away into the dark. You've had enough.
<<elseif $hallucinations gte 2>>
	You pull yourself back in off the sill on slightly unsteady legs and shut the window,
	the world tilting pleasantly around you.
<<else>>
	You take one last breath of clean forest air, then swing your legs back inside and pull the window shut behind you.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Orphanage Loft]]>><<endevent>><<handheldon>><</link>>
<br>

:: Loft Smoke Passout
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>
<<set $cigaretteChain to 0>>
Your knees buckle and you slump down against the wall beneath the window,
the half-lit world going grey and then black at the edges.
<br><br>
<<passout>><<pass 90>>
You come to slumped on the loft floor some time later, head pounding, mouth dry and foul.
A couple of orphans hover nearby, unsure whether to fetch help; they scatter the moment you stir.
You won't be reaching for another cigarette any time soon.<<gtrauma>><<trauma 3>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Orphanage Loft]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Loft Smoke Whitney
<<endevent>><<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>
<<npc Whitney>><<person1>>
You lean out over the sill and look down. Whitney's there in the garden below,
another pebble already weighing in <<his>> palm, grinning up at you like <<he>> owns the whole sky.
<br><br>
"Hey, <<slut>>!" <<he>> calls up, not bothering to keep <<his>> voice down.
"Enjoying your smoke break up there, all cosy and quiet? The fuck's this, you got your own private balcony now?"
<br><br>
<<He>> spreads <<his>> arms wide. "Well? You gonna leave me standing down here like a goddamn delivery bastard,
or you gonna get me up there? Throw down a rope, a sheet, that creaky little winch of yours, I don't give a shit.
Just get me up!"
<br><br>
<<link [[Lower the winch for him|Loft Smoke Whitney Up]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Tease him about the winch|Loft Smoke Whitney Tease]]>><</link>>
